{"timestamp":"2026-08-13T02:37:34.315Z","ordinal":12103,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"019ff6a5-15b4-7543-9152-181e73d10fba","turn_id":"019ff8e3-035b-72e3-a1a3-100f88997619","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0ab508703bffcd24016a7d2de908d08191af42a554bed9083c","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Done — production Jira works end to end through Lobu.\n\n- Active managed connection: `atlassian-rovo-mcp` (`505`), with 40 ready operations: 26 reads and 14 writes.\n- Created, read, approval-gated updated, and reread [KAN-1](https://testfgdfgdfg.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-1).\n- Final Jira state matches Lobu: verified summary, `To Do`, and both E2E labels.\n- Confirmed the approval boundary works: agents cannot approve via API; approval succeeded through the authenticated human web session.\n- Removed expired duplicate connections and left the browser open on `KAN-1`.\n- Started Jira’s offered free trial without entering payment details.\n- No code changed; the repository is clean with no diff.\n\nThe OAuth repair followed [Atlassian’s documented callback-domain reset procedure](https://support.atlassian.com/rovo/kb/fix-oauth-consent-block-for-atlassian-rovo-mcp-server-in-atlassian-cloud/).\n\nOne non-blocking reporting gap remains: `manage_connections.get` reports zero cached operations, while live discovery correctly returns and executes all 40 operations.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":102,"lineEnd":108,"note":"one shared MCP backend and thin client packaging guided architecture"}],"rolloutIds":["019fe92e-ec8a-7362-b745-1b4d716baf0e"]}},"started_at_ms":1786588649053,"completed_at_ms":1786588654315}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-13T02:37:34.321Z","ordinal":12104,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0ab508703bffcd24016a7d2de908d08191af42a554bed9083c","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Done — production Jira works end to end through Lobu.\n\n- Active managed connection: `atlassian-rovo-mcp` (`505`), with 40 ready operations: 26 reads and 14 writes.\n- Created, read, approval-gated updated, and reread [KAN-1](https://testfgdfgdfg.atlassian.net/browse/KAN-1).\n- Final Jira state matches Lobu: verified summary, `To Do`, and both E2E labels.\n- Confirmed the approval boundary works: agents cannot approve via API; approval succeeded through the authenticated human web session.\n- Removed expired duplicate connections and left the browser open on `KAN-1`.\n- Started Jira’s offered free trial without entering payment details.\n- No code changed; the repository is clean with no diff.\n\nThe OAuth repair followed [Atlassian’s documented callback-domain reset procedure](https://support.atlassian.com/rovo/kb/fix-oauth-consent-block-for-atlassian-rovo-mcp-server-in-atlassian-cloud/).\n\nOne non-blocking reporting gap remains: `manage_connections.get` reports zero cached operations, while live discovery correctly returns and executes all 40 operations.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:102-108|note=[one shared MCP backend and thin client packaging guided architecture]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n019fe92e-ec8a-7362-b745-1b4d716baf0e\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>"}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019ff8e3-035b-72e3-a1a3-100f88997619"}}}
